 "alt": "Three old ways of carrying news: a messenger on a horse, who managed about a hundred and sixty kilometres a day and was the limit for three thousand years; towers on hilltops with arms read through a telescope, which carried a short sentence across France in two hours but could not work at night or in fog; and the telegraph, the real break, because it was the first time a message could move without anything moving.",
